PASS | fort-stewart | FAQ JSON-LD == visible Q&A | page/src=[('Does Hunter Army Airfield get Fort Stewart BAH?', 'No. Hunter Army Airfield (ZIP 31409) is in Savannah, which DTMO puts in a separate housing area, SAVANNAH, GA (GA077), with its own rates. Fort Stewart and Hinesville (31313) are in FORT STEWART, GA (GA080).'), ('Does 2026 BAH at Fort Stewart cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With typical 3-bedroom rent of $1,200–$1,550 and utilities of about $270–$515 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($2,310) lands between $245 and $840 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2026 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')] | ref=[('Does Hunter Army Airfield get Fort Stewart BAH?', 'No. Hunter Army Airfield (ZIP 31409) is in Savannah, which DTMO puts in a separate housing area, SAVANNAH, GA (GA077), with its own rates. Fort Stewart and Hinesville (31313) are in FORT STEWART, GA (GA080).'), ('Does 2026 BAH at Fort Stewart cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With typical 3-bedroom rent of $1,200–$1,550 and utilities of about $270–$515 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($2,310) lands between $245 and $840 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2026 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')]
