PASS | joint-base-san-antonio | FAQ JSON-LD == visible Q&A | page/src=[('Do Fort Sam Houston, Lackland and Randolph all get the same BAH?', 'Yes. ZIPs 78234 (JBSA-Fort Sam Houston), 78236 (JBSA-Lackland) and 78150 (JBSA-Randolph) all map to the SAN ANTONIO, TX housing area (TX285), so all three use these rates.'), ('Does 2026 BAH at Joint Base San Antonio cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With typical 3-bedroom rent of $1,400–$1,950 and utilities of about $255–$500 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($1,869) lands between −$581 and $214 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2026 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')] | ref=[('Do Fort Sam Houston, Lackland and Randolph all get the same BAH?', 'Yes. ZIPs 78234 (JBSA-Fort Sam Houston), 78236 (JBSA-Lackland) and 78150 (JBSA-Randolph) all map to the SAN ANTONIO, TX housing area (TX285), so all three use these rates.'), ('Does 2026 BAH at Joint Base San Antonio cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With typical 3-bedroom rent of $1,400–$1,950 and utilities of about $255–$500 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($1,869) lands between −$581 and $214 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2026 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')]
