PASS | schofield-barracks | FAQ JSON-LD == visible Q&A | page/src=[('Do all Oahu posts get the same BAH?', 'Yes. Schofield Barracks (96857), Wahiawa (96786), Fort Shafter (96858), Joint Base Pearl Harbor-Hickam (96853, 96860) and Marine Corps Base Hawaii (96863) all map to HONOLULU COUNTY, HI (HI408).'), ('Do I get COLA on top of BAH at Schofield Barracks?', 'Yes. Hawaii duty stations get BAH plus a cost-of-living allowance (COLA), which DTMO sets separately by rank, years of service and dependents. This page shows BAH only; the calculator adds COLA for Schofield Barracks.'), ('Does 2026 BAH at Schofield Barracks cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With typical 3-bedroom rent of $2,500–$3,500 and utilities of about $320–$610 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($3,663) lands between −$447 and $843 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2026 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')] | ref=[('Do all Oahu posts get the same BAH?', 'Yes. Schofield Barracks (96857), Wahiawa (96786), Fort Shafter (96858), Joint Base Pearl Harbor-Hickam (96853, 96860) and Marine Corps Base Hawaii (96863) all map to HONOLULU COUNTY, HI (HI408).'), ('Do I get COLA on top of BAH at Schofield Barracks?', 'Yes. Hawaii duty stations get BAH plus a cost-of-living allowance (COLA), which DTMO sets separately by rank, years of service and dependents. This page shows BAH only; the calculator adds COLA for Schofield Barracks.'), ('Does 2026 BAH at Schofield Barracks cover rent and utilities?', 'It depends on rank. With typical 3-bedroom rent of $2,500–$3,500 and utilities of about $320–$610 a month, a Sergeant (E-5) with dependents ($3,663) lands between −$447 and $843 a month after housing. These are planning estimates, not official figures.'), ('Do I get a different rate if I live in a nearby town?', 'No. BAH follows your permanent duty-station ZIP, not your home address.'), ('When do these rates apply?', 'These are the calendar-year 2026 rates. Rate protection keeps your rate from dropping while you stay at the same post with the same status; a PCS, a reduction in grade or a change in dependency status resets it. DTMO usually publishes the next year’s rates in mid-December.')]
